<<~ ahu slot=`#/purpose`>>

!! The Crest

`takeCrest` removes whole families from the queue head in order, weighing count, bytes and operations against the caller's limits. The first family always rides, even when it exceeds a limit, so the queue advances without splitting a family. `adaptDepth` shrinks or grows the next depth from observed and target duration, bounds each step, and respects the caller's ceiling. `scaleLimits` applies a depth ratio across the axes. Callers use `yieldToHost` from `host-task.ts` between waves; this module reads no clock and schedules no host task.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/law`>>

!! Nalu Law

The crest enacts whole-family slicing and host pacing under <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/nalu#/the-wave-shape`>>. The wiki's own dispatch still decides the observer delivery boundary.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/callers`>>

!! Callers

`WaveLanding` in lararium-tw5 slices changes on count; the lararium-node ingest settle slices carriers, encoded bytes and estimated objects and adapts depth. `ingest-wave-budget.ts` consumes `fitsWave` and the weight types. `gate-tuning.ts#adaptGate` calls `adaptDepth` for the flush-gate servo. Capture flush slicing and the autosync wait remain next candidates.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/caps-cost`>>

!! Caps and Cost

The caller supplies count, byte and operation caps; an oversized first family travels alone. The servo clamps its step and ceiling, and depth stays at least one. Slicing weighs each examined family and shifts the queue; array shifts can move remaining entries. The module carries no dependencies or clock, and callers pay for weighing, applying and yielding.

<<~/ahu>>

